            <ArticleTitle>Pulmonary infection with Mycobacterium neoaurum identified by 16S ribosomal DNA sequence.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e227-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Mycobacterium neoaurum infection has rarely been found in humans, and only a limited number of cases have been reported. We describe the first case of pulmonary infection with M. neoaurum. We speculate that unrecognized aspiration and long-term corticosteroid therapy predisposed our patient to this rare mycobacterial infection.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
